## Prior art and related projects

The design of this repository was informed by work done in a sibling project of ours,
[`dsh-harmonyos-hiboard`](https://github.com/MaybeMeibeMaybi/dsh-harmonyos-hiboard), which in
turn is based on [Entity-Him/dsh-hiboard-push](https://github.com/Entity-Him/dsh-hiboard-push)
(MIT). Two patterns were carried over from there:

1. **Starting a helper process from a dsh profile plugin** (`ctx.effect` + `spawn` with
   `detached` + `unref`, health-probe before spawning) rather than from an external
   launcher or scheduled task. The sibling project uses it to start a reverse proxy; this
   project uses the same pattern for the LAN entry proxy.

2. **The Windows script-encoding rules** documented in `docs/DEPLOY.md`: `.cmd`/`.bat` must
   be ASCII-only (cmd.exe decodes them with the system ANSI code page, so UTF-8 text becomes
   mojibake and eats the leading `REM`), and a `.ps1` containing non-ASCII must carry a
   UTF-8 BOM (PowerShell 5.1 decodes it as ANSI otherwise). These were learned the hard way
   and are recorded so that nobody has to rediscover them.

No third-party source files are vendored in this repository.

## Runtime dependencies

- Node.js 18+ (built-in modules only: `node:http`, `node:os`)
- DeepSeek Harness (dsh) with cordis 4, for the plugin
- `@deepseek-ai/schemastery`, for the plugin's config schema (peer dependency)
